The bowling alley glowed in neon purples and blues, everything shimmering under the blacklights Ava’s ribbon especially, glowing like a tiny pastel halo. Rowan sprinted ahead like a child. Jamie followed with the patience of someone who regretted every life choice. Ava stood at the lane holding a lilac bowling ball that looked way too big for her.

<<ava "I… um… don’t actually know how to bowl." >>

<<leo "It’s okay. Just try." >>

She stepped forward, swung her arm and the ball instantly curved into the gutter. She gasped.

<<ava "Oh no  I-I killed the ball " >>

Rowan cackled.

<<rowan "Welcome to bowling hell!" >>

Ava pouted at him, then turned to me, cheeks warm.

<<ava "I-I really am terrible." >>

I moved behind her, gently placing my hands on her hips.

<<leo "Let me show you." >>

She stiffened for a second then slowly relaxed into my chest, breath soft.

<<ava "O-Okay… guide me?" >>

I slid one hand along her arm to adjust her elbow, the other staying at her waist. She leaned back slightly, fitting against me like she belonged there.

<<leo "Swing slower. Keep your wrist straight." >>

<<ava "Like this?" >>

<<leo "Perfect. Try again." >>

She stepped forward and released. The ball rolled straight slow, wobbly clink. It hit one lonely pin on the far right. Ava gasped and spun around.

<<ava "I HIT ONE!" >>

Then she launched herself into a hug quick, impulsive, warm. Her arms wrapped around my waist; her cheek pressed to my chest.

<<ava "Leo, I hit one!" >>

I laughed softly, holding her back.

<<leo "You did amazing." >>

She pulled away, but not far. Just enough to look up at me eyes bright, soft, glowing. Her softness returned. The same softness from before everything fell apart. The same softness from the early days. Jamie threw her ball next: another perfect strike. Rowan groaned.

<<rowan "WHY is she good at everything " >>

Jamie stuck her tongue out at him.

<<jamie "Skill. Talent. Grace." >>

Ava giggled and tugged at my sleeve, guiding me to sit beside her on the bench. She held her soda with both hands, sipping, then nudged it toward me.

<<ava "D-Do you want some?" >>

<<leo "Sure." >>

I took a sip. She watched my mouth as I handed it back eyes lingering for half a second longer than necessary. Then she scooted closer.

Not subtly. Not nervously. Just… wanting to be close. Her shoulder pressed to mine. Her thigh brushed my leg. Her head tilted toward my arm.

<<ava "This is fun…" >>

<<leo "Yeah. It is." >>

She looked up at me, voice a whisper.

<<ava "I feel… safe with you today." >>

She rested her hand on my thigh gentle, shy, but openly affectionate. For the first time all week, she wasn’t scared of her own feelings… or mine.

[[Leave the bowling alley|day_4_9]]


:: day_4_9

We left the bowling alley still laughing over Rowan’s eighth gutter ball, but the farther we moved from neon lights and noisy lanes, the quieter Ava became.

The four of us turned the corner toward the VR district laughing, bags rustling when Rowan suddenly stopped dead in his tracks.

<<rowan "HOOOOLY  look at THAT." >>

Before I even saw what he meant, Jamie groaned.

<<jamie "Rowan. Don’t." >>

Then I saw it. A bright neon storefront glowing like a sinful lighthouse,

<span style="color: pink; font-size: 30px;">PINK PLANET - ADULTS ONLY</span>

Window display overflowing with vibrators the size of small dragons and lingerie that looked like it came from a boss fight.

Ava froze beside me. Completely froze. Her hand shot to my sleeve instantly, gripping it like she was about to be swept out to sea.

<<ava "L-Leo why why is it so BRIGHT " >>

Before I could answer, Rowan pointed dramatically at the window.

<<rowan "Bro. Look at the SIZE of that one. That’s a legendary-tier weapon." >>

Ava made a noise I’d never heard before like a dying kettle and buried her face in my arm.

<<ava "No no no no don’t describe it don’t describe it " >>

Jamie smacked Rowan’s shoulder with her bag.

<<jamie "STOP TALKING. YOU’RE TRAUMATIZING MY CHILD." >>

<<rowan "I’m educating the youth!" >>

<<jamie "YOU’RE MAKING IT WORSE." >>

A passing couple glanced over. Ava squeaked and hid even deeper against me, clutching my sleeve like her life depended on it.

<<ava "Why is it in the WINDOW? Wh why would they put that OUTSIDE " >>

I stroked her arm lightly.

<<leo "It’s okay, just… don’t look." >>

<<ava "I DID look " >>

Rowan leaned closer to the glass.

<<rowan "No seriously, how does anyone even " >>

<<jamie "ROWAN, I SWEAR TO GOD " >>

She yanked him away by the hood. He stumbled backward, laughing like an idiot.

<<rowan "I’m just saying, that one has recoil " >>

<<jamie "YOU DON’T EVEN KNOW WHAT THAT MEANS " >>

Ava gave a tiny distressed whimper.

<<ava "Leo, please tell them to stop " >>

I guided her past the store gently, shielding her from the window with my body.

<<leo "Hey. We’re already past it. You’re okay." >>

She peeked out from behind my arm, face red enough to catch fire.

<<ava "Why do stores like that exist in the MIDDLE of the mall?" >>

Jamie sighed dramatically.

<<jamie "Capitalism, sweetheart." >>

Rowan gave a thumbs-up.

<<rowan "And horny adults." >>

Jamie smacked him again. Ava clung to me the entire walk until the neon glow was far behind us. She finally loosened her grip but kept my sleeve lightly between her fingers.

<<ava "…I am never walking near that place again." >>

<<leo "I’ll steer you away next time." >>

She nodded quickly, cheeks pink but smiling now tiny, embarrassed, adorable.

<<ava "Thank you…" >>

Rowan, still rubbing his shoulder from Jamie’s smack, grinned.

<<rowan "Honestly? Best part of the mall so far." >>

Jamie glared.

<<jamie "Say one more word about vibrators and I will put you in the trash can." >>

Ava buried her face and laughed quietly against my arm and just like that, the panic melted away. The group felt whole again chaotic, loud, ridiculous but together.

[[Go to VR Store|day_4_10]]


:: day_4_10

The closer we got to the VR district, the quieter Ava became. She tugged at her ribbon, gaze lowered.

<<leo "Ava?" >>

She startled lightly.

<<ava "I’m okay. Just… nervous." >>

I took her hand. She held it immediately. Rowan stepped behind us and shoved my shoulder dramatically.

<<rowan "Forward, chosen ones! Into the future!" >>

<<leo "Please don’t narrate us." >>

<<rowan "Too late." >>

Jamie laughed softly.

<<jamie "Sweetheart, it’s not scary. Just high-tech mood lighting." >>

Ava nodded, but her fingers tightened around me. The doors slid open with a soft hiss. Inside felt like a different world: dark glass, cool blue light spilling across the floor, pods lined along the wall. Ava took one shaky step inside, eyes huge.

<<ava "…It looks like a spaceship." >>

I squeezed her sleeve gently.

<<leo "Yeah. It’s unreal." >>

Rowan wandered toward a display and poked a helmet.

<<rowan "This one definitely absorbs souls." >>

Jamie smacked his arm.

<<jamie "Stop being weird." >>

A tiny giggle escaped Ava quiet, nervous, but real. A store agent approached warm smile, sleek uniform.

<<agent "Welcome! First time exploring immersive VR?" >>

Ava immediately tried hiding behind me.

<<leo "Yeah. We’re new." >>

The agent nodded warmly.

<<agent "Perfect. I’ll guide you through it. Everything here adapts to your comfort level." >>

Ava peeked out.

<<ava "…Adapts?" >>

<<agent "Yes. The system mirrors your emotional state, easing or intensifying gently based on what you want." >>

Jamie tapped Ava’s arm.

<<jamie "It helped us a lot. It’s safer than it looks." >>

Rowan pointed to a device.

<<rowan "Except that one. Don’t trust that one." >>

<<jamie "Rowan, that’s a foot massager." >>

Ava laughed again softer this time. The agent gestured forward.

<<agent "Let me show you the basics. No pressure." >>

Ava nodded, gripping my sleeve.

<<ava "Leo… stay close?" >>

<<leo "I’m not going anywhere." >>

Together, we stepped deeper into the glowing hall.

[[Follow the agent|day_4_11]]



:: day_4_11

The agent led us onto a circular platform surrounded by curved screens. Ava stepped closer to me, fingers sliding down from my sleeve until she held my wrist fully.

<<ava "It looks… complicated." >>

<<leo "Complicated isn’t dangerous." >>

<<jamie "Exactly. Just listen. It’s gentler than it looks." >>

The screens lit up all at once bright landscapes, cities, faces. Ava flinched and bumped into my side.

<<leo "Hey. I’ve got you." >>

She nodded shakily and clung to my hand. The agent smiled.

<<agent "This system uses brainwave simulation. It tracks sensation, movement, emotional response. Everything feels real because your mind treats it as real." >>

Ava’s eyes widened.

<<ava "Real…?" >>

<<agent "Real, but safe. It adapts instantly if you’re overwhelmed." >>

Rowan muttered loudly.

<<rowan "Very good news for the anxiety-prone among us. Jamie." >>

<<jamie "Rowan, you are anxiety." >>

Ava laughed softly relieved for a second. The agent continued, tapping the display again.

<<agent "You don’t move your real body in VR. Your brain sends signals directly to your avatar. Same with touch: all sensation is virtual, not physical." >>

<<agent "While you are inside, every input sensation like smell, touch, sound, visuals, taste all coming from virtual space. Same as that every output, like evreything you are trying to do will happen in virtual world untill you log out." >>

<<agent "Everything inside also feels like same or more than that in real world. You can't even tell the difference..">>

Ava swallowed.

<<ava "So… it listens to you?" >>

<<agent "Exactly. Every emotion. Every hesitation. It’s designed to respond gently and personally." >>

Jamie nodded.

<<jamie "It’s why I never panicked inside. It reacts faster than you can think." >>

Rowan nodded.

<<rowan "Yeah, it caught me before I faceplanted once." >>

<<jamie "You tripped over nothing." >>

The agent brought up a sky panorama too vivid, too crisp.

<<agent "VR can render at double human optical limits. Many people say it looks more real than life." >>

Ava let out a tiny breath.

<<ava "It’s… beautiful." >>

I squeezed her hand.

<<leo "We’ll go slow. Whatever pace you want." >>

She leaned into me, tension easing a little. But then,

<<agent "Some users build full lives in VR families, relationships because it’s so immersive." >>

Ava stiffened, fingers clenching mine.

<<ava "L-Lives?" >>

<<leo "Hey. Just options. Not expectations." >>

She nodded, breath shaky but steadying.

<<agent "Everything is personalized. Nothing happens without your permission." >>

Ava finally exhaled.

<<ava "Okay… good." >>

Her grip softened not letting go, just trusting.

[[Watch the screen|day_4_12]]

:: day_4_12

The screens shifted again bright fractal lines becoming soft silhouettes shaped like people, pulsing with colored light. Ava stiffened.

<<ava "What… is that?" >>

<<agent "Emotional mapping. It shows how the system reads comfort, fear, curiosity, excitement." >>

A silhouette glowed gold when “touched,” blue when another approached, red when it reached out. Ava watched, breath shaky. Jamie stepped close.

<<jamie "It’s not reading secrets, sweetheart. Just safety." >>

Ava nodded, but her grip on my hand tightened. The agent tapped again, and two blurry avatar forms appeared.

<<ava "Those… are us?" >>

<<agent "Placeholders. Your real avatars form after the scan based on what feels natural to you." >>

Ava swallowed.

<<ava "Natural…?" >>

<<agent "The version of you without fear or pressure. Shape follows instinct, not anxiety." >>

Ava’s knees almost buckled, and I held her waist lightly.

<<leo "I’m right here." >>

She leaned into me, whispering:

<<ava "I don’t know what that version of me even is…" >>

<<leo "I think she’s braver than you realize." >>

A slow breath left her, trembling but lighter. The agent continued gently.

<<agent "You can adjust everything intimacy filters, sensation limits, emotional dampeners. Nothing happens without your active yes." >>

Ava lifted her head.

<<ava "Filters… like turning things down?" >>

<<agent "Exactly. If intensity is too much, it softens instantly. If you freeze, it pauses. If you panic, it stops." >>

Jamie placed a hand on her back.

<<jamie "VR won’t do what your body does when you’re scared. You won’t freeze." >>

Rowan raised a hand.

<<rowan "Emotion buffer mode is a literal lifesaver. Don’t turn it off unless you want chaos." >>

Jamie smacked him.

<<jamie "You caused the chaos." >>

Ava giggled really giggled for the first time in the store. Then the screens changed again: two avatars stepping closer, surrounded by soft glowing light, leaning in with intimate energy.

Ava froze. Her hand slipped from mine and went straight to her ribbon. Her voice cracked.

<<ava "L-Leo… would I have to… do stuff like that?" >>

I turned toward her.

<<leo "No. Never. Not unless you choose it. Not here. Not anywhere." >>

Her eyes softened but filled.

<<ava "But… if I wanted to… would I still freeze?" >>

That one hit deep. I cupped her hand gently.

<<leo "VR won’t let fear take over. You control every second." >>

Jamie nodded, voice low and warm.

<<jamie "You’d get to feel free. Safe. Not stuck inside your body." >>

Ava’s eyes shimmered fear, hope, longing all at once.

<<agent "VR lets you meet the version of yourself you’ve never been allowed to be." >>

A shiver ran through Ava not fear, but wonder. She reached for my hand again, this time holding tight. She didn’t let go.

[[Go to Scan Room|day_4_14]]

:: day_4_14

The scan room was quiet cool light, two tall pods pulsing gently like metallic cocoons. Ava stopped the moment she saw them. Her fingers tightened in mine.

<<ava "They… look a little scary." >>

Jamie touched her shoulder.

<<jamie "They’re harmless. Like standing in warm air." >>

I stepped closer, brushing her hand with my thumb.

<<leo "We do it together. I’m right next to you." >>

Ava nodded, still nervous but trusting. The agent gestured to the pods.

<<agent "These scan posture, body proportions, micro-expressions, and emotional patterns. All for comfort settings only." >>

Ava blinked.

<<ava "It sees… everything?" >>

<<agent "Only what you allow your avatar to show." >>

Rowan grinned.

<<rowan "Mine gave me bonus abs. Best bug ever." >>

Ava let out a tiny nervous laugh softening just enough to step closer to the pod. I opened mine and glanced over.

<<leo "Ready?" >>

<<ava "…As I’ll ever be." >>

We stepped inside. The doors closed. Inside the scan White light filled the chamber. A soft chime.

<<system "Initializing physical scan. Please remain still.">>

I stayed steady, hands at my sides. Then I heard it A tiny gasp from Ava’s pod. I turned just enough to see her through the side panel: fists curled, knees together, shoulders tight. The scan light washed over her like gentle waves. Her ribbon glowed softly. She looked delicate. She looked brave.

She saw me watching. Lifted her fingers. Pressed them to the glass. Small. Shy. Reaching. I pressed my palm to my side of the glass. Close as the pod allowed. The system continued,

<<system "Posture mapping complete.">>

<<system "Recording micro-expressions.">>

<<system "Initiating neural waveform registration.">>

Ava stiffened, breath fogging the glass. She closed her eyes, trembling. I whispered even though she couldn’t hear:

<<leo "You’re doing perfect." >>

She exhaled, slow. Her shoulders lowered. Her outline glowed gold as the scan completed.

<<system "Scan complete. Preparing data sets.">>

My pod opened first; hers followed with a soft hiss. Ava stepped out quickly and went straight to me, fingers bunching in my shirt.

<<ava "Did I… do it right?" >>

<<leo "Perfectly." >>

Her breath steadied. Jamie clapped.

<<jamie "See? Easy." >>

Rowan smirked.

<<rowan "You two looked like baby deer learning gravity." >>

Ava groaned and hid her face in my arm. The agent approached with a sleek black case.

<<agent "Your scans are complete. Now choose the world you'd like to begin with." >>

The holographic panels flashed to life in front of us. Ava and I stepped forward together, still holding hands.

[[Browse the games|day_4_15]]

:: day_4_15

The agent tapped the first holographic panel. Color exploded across it floating continents, glowing forests, waterfalls spilling into clouds lit like molten stars. Ava’s hand tightened around mine.

<<ava "…Oh." >>

Soft. Breathless. The title shimmered overhead:

<span style="color: yellow; font-size: 30px;">LUMIRA: REALMS OF THE ETERNAL SKY</span>

<<img "images/scene/part_1/lumira.jpeg" "header">>

<<img "images/scene/part_1/lumira_2.jpeg" "header">>

<<img "images/scene/part_1/lumira_3.jpeg" "header">>

<<img "images/scene/part_1/lumira_4.jpeg" "header">>

<<img "images/scene/part_1/lumira_5.jpeg" "header">>

<<img "images/scene/part_1/lumira_6.jpeg" "header">>

<<img "images/scene/part_1/lumira_7.jpeg" "header">>

<<img "images/scene/part_1/lumira_8.jpeg" "header">>

<<agent "Our flagship fantasy immersion. Perfect for exploration, emotional resonance, and gentle intimacy." >>

I stepped closer, mesmerized.

<<leo "This looks unreal." >>

Rowan leaned in, grinning like an idiot.

<<rowan "Lumira is what happens when a fantasy novel takes drugs." >>

<<jamie "Ignore him." >>

Ava giggled behind her hand small, shy, wonder warming her cheeks. The preview shifted. Two avatars walked side-by-side in a glowing forest hands almost touching. Wisps of golden light curled around their wrists, reacting to their emotions. Ava gasped.

<<img "images/scene/part_1/lumira_9.jpeg" "header">>

<<ava "Leo… look…" >>

<<agent "In Lumira, magic mirrors connection. If trust grows, the light grows. If someone feels overwhelmed, it fades." >>

<<ava "It listens to you…" >>

I squeezed her hand.

<<leo "Feels like a world made for you." >>

<<ava "M–me?" >>

<<leo "You love magic more than reality. This fits." >>

Her blush deepened; she didn’t deny it. The hologram changed again A floating citadel, two avatars sparring gently, light tracing every movement.

<<ava "It feels… safe." >>

Something in my chest loosened.

<<agent "Lumira is chosen by most couples who want closeness without any pressure." >>

Jamie nudged Ava gently.

<<jamie "It’s basically a romance novel you walk around inside." >>

<<ava "Like… the warrior-mage ones?" >>

<<jamie "Exactly." >>

Ava stared at the floating world soft awe, blooming hope, a little longing. She didn’t speak. She just squeezed my hand tighter and leaned into my arm. Just a breath. Just enough to say, I want this.

[[Select the Lumira|day_4_16]]


:: day_4_16

The hologram dimmed into a gentle rotation of Lumira’s sky-islands. Ava stared at it, lips parted, fingers lightly trembling in mine.

<<ava "…It’s really beautiful." >>

<<leo "Yeah. It feels… right." >>

Rowan threw his arms up.

<<rowan "I vote Lumira. Zero thought required." >>

Jamie elbowed him.

<<jamie "This isn’t your VR arc, idiot. Let them talk." >>

Ava kept watching the golden magic curling around the avatar hands.

<<ava "The way it reacts… it’s so soft. Like it wouldn’t… push." >>

<<leo "Exactly. No pressure. No forcing anything." >>

She swallowed.

<<ava "And… the magic changes based on… feelings?" >>

<<agent "Yes. Your emotional resonance defines the intensity. It protects you from discomfort and amplifies comfort." >>

Ava’s shoulders dropped a little relief, amazement, fear melting together.

<<ava "That sounds… safe. Safe in a way real life hasn’t been." >>

I stepped closer, tilting my head.

<<leo "Do you feel drawn to it?" >>

She hesitated then nodded, almost shyly.

<<ava "I do. I really… really do." >>

Rowan leaned in dramatically.

<<rowan "Then boom. Decision made. Sky world. Floaty rocks. Magic hugs." >>

Jamie pinched him.

<<jamie "Stop narrating." >>

Ava giggled soft, genuine and turned back to me.

<<ava "What about you? Do you want Lumira?" >>

I smiled.

<<leo "If you feel safe there? That’s where I want to be." >>

Her cheeks warmed at that slow pink rising down her neck.

<<ava "I… like the idea of us exploring a world like this. Together." >>

<<leo "Then let’s choose it." >>

She took a breath steady, hopeful and nodded with new conviction.

<<ava "Okay. Then… Lumira." >>

The agent clapped gently, pleased.

<<agent "Wonderful choice. I’ll prepare your starter setup and sync your scans to the Lumira core." >>

Rowan lifted his hands like he was blessing a ceremony.

<<rowan "Welcome to Team Lumira, children." >>

Jamie sighed.

<<jamie "Ignore him, again." >>

Ava squeezed my hand quiet, steady, grateful.

<<ava "Leo… thank you for helping me choose." >>

<<leo "You chose it. I’m just walking in with you." >>

She smiled at me soft, glowing, braver than she realized.

[[Finalize the purchase|day_4_17]]


:: day_4_17

The Lumira hologram faded, leaving the soft blue glow of the VR store around us. Ava was still holding my hand looser now, not trembling. Just warm. The agent returned with a sleek black case and two wrist bands.

<<agent "We’ll finalize your purchase at the main counter. Everything is already synced to your scans." >>

<<rowan "Translation: You two are officially entering gamer marriage." >>

<<jamie "Rowan, they’re buying VR, not eloping." >>

<<rowan "Same vibe." >>

Ava turned bright red.

<<ava "R-Rowan !" >>

I slipped my hand to her waist lightly.

<<leo "Ignore him. Everyone else does." >>

<<rowan "HEY." >>

Ava giggled, the sound small but real. At the Counter. The agent set the case down with a soft click.

<<agent "Your package includes the dual-immersion set, sensory adapters, and entry-level Lumira access. You can upgrade later, but this is more than enough to begin." >>

Ava touched the case gently, almost reverently.

<<ava "It’s… real now." >>

<<leo "Yeah. We actually did it." >>

She nodded, eyes softening.

<<ava "We did." >>

The agent tapped a screen.

<<agent "Your total is 5000" >>

Rowan slapped his card onto the counter dramatically.

<<rowan "Put my discount code in. I didn’t grind thirty VR tournaments for nothing." >>

Jamie pulled him back by the hood.

<<jamie "Stop trying to look cool. Let them pay normally." >>

<<rowan "I am cool " >>

<<jamie "No." >>

Ava covered her mouth, laughing into her fingers. The store’s glow lit her face beautifully. I paid simple, quiet, my heart beating too fast as the receipt printed. The agent handed the case to me.

<<agent "Congratulations. Lumira will be available to you immediately when you initialize at home." >>

<<ava "Th… thank you." >>

She dipped a tiny bow out of instinct. The agent smiled warmly. Leaving the Store As we stepped back into the mall hallway, Ava walked a little closer not clutching, not scared. Just near.

<<ava "Leo?" >>

<<leo "Yeah?" >>

She looked at the VR case in my hand… then at me.

<<ava "I’m… excited. And scared. But mostly excited." >>

I squeezed her hand.

<<leo "Me too." >>

Rowan leaned over my shoulder.

<<rowan "Wow. Emotional maturity. Couldn’t be me." >>

<<jamie "We know." >>

Ava giggled again light, unguarded. She looked up at me one more time, eyes shining with something warm and new.

<<ava "Thank you… for choosing this with me." >>

<<leo "Always." >>

Her fingers slip between mine fully no hesitation this time and together, carrying the VR that might change everything, we walked back toward the mall’s main wing.

[[Walk to Campus|day_4_18]]



:: day_4_18
<<set $locationImage = "images/locations/night.jpeg">>
We stepped out of the mall into late-afternoon light soft gold drifting across the pavement. Ava stayed close to me, her shoulder brushing mine as she hugged her bag gently to her chest. The VR case swung lightly in my hand, heavier in meaning than weight. Rowan stretched his arms over his head.

<<rowan "Alright, children. We have fed you, entertained you, educated you, and prevented you from spontaneously combusting. Our job here is done." >>

Jamie snorted.

<<jamie "Translation: Rowan wants bubble tea before he dies." >>

<<rowan "I need it, Jamie. It’s medical." >>

Ava giggled, the sound small but sweet. She shifted closer to me, whispering.

<<ava "They’re… loud today." >>

<<leo "They’re always loud." >>

<<ava "Mm… but in a nice way." >>

Rowan pointed dramatically at us as we walked.

<<rowan "Hey. Before we split proud of you two. For real." >>

Ava immediately flustered.

<<ava "W-What? Why ?" >>

<<rowan "You bought VR. That’s emotional adulthood. You’re basically leveling up." >>

Jamie groaned.

<<jamie "Ignore him. What he means is… you handled today really well, Ava." >>

Ava’s head dropped shyly.

<<ava "I… I tried." >>

<<jamie "You did more than try." >>

She reached to squeeze Ava’s shoulder gently.

<<jamie "You were brave. And soft. And honest. That’s what matters." >>

Ava swallowed, voice tiny.

<<ava "…Thank you." >>

Rowan clapped me on the back.

<<rowan "Leo. Don’t break anything when you set it up." >>

<<leo "I’m not you." >>

<<rowan "Wow. Hurtful and true." >>

Jamie tugged his sleeve.

<<jamie "We’re heading this way. You two go rest you’ve had a big day." >>

Ava nodded, bowing slightly.

<<ava "Thank you… for everything." >>

<<jamie "Anytime, sweetheart." >>

They exchanged one more warm smile before Rowan saluted dramatically.

<<rowan "Fare thee well, VR virgins! See you tomorrow!" >>

<<jamie "ROWAN " >>

Their bickering trailed off as they walked in the opposite direction… leaving just me and Ava in the slowly cooling air. Ava watched them go, then let out a soft breath.

<<ava "It feels quieter now…" >>

She reached for my hand unprompted, gentle and intertwined our fingers.

<<ava "…but not in a bad way." >>

I squeezed back.

<<leo "Let’s head to campus?" >>

She nodded, ribbon fluttering slightly as she leaned closer.

<<ava "Yes. Let’s… go to campus." >>

Together we continued toward campus, the weight of the VR case between us like a quiet promise of what was coming next.

[[Walk to Ava's Dorm Room|day_4_19]]

:: day_4_19
<<set $locationImage = "images/locations/ava_dorm.jpeg">>
We reached Ava’s dorm as the sky dimmed into a warm evening blur. She unlocked the door, stepped inside, then leaned her back against it exhaling like the whole day finally caught up to her. Her ribbon drooped a little. Her shoulders loosened.

<<ava "…I’m tired." >>

Her voice was small, honest.

<<ava "Today was… a lot. In a good way. But still… a lot." >>

I nodded, setting the VR case gently on her desk.

<<leo "Yeah. It was a big day." >>

She rubbed her eyes with her sleeve, adorable and exhausted.

<<ava "I don’t think I can… start VR tonight. My brain feels like pudding." >>

She peeked up at me through her hair.

<<ava "Is… that okay?" >>

I stepped closer, smiling softly.

<<leo "Ava, of course it’s okay. We don’t have to rush anything." >>

Her body eased subtle, grateful. But then she fidgeted with her ribbon, hesitating.

<<ava "But… um… Leo?" >>

<<leo "Mm?" >>

She nudged the VR case with her toe, cheeks pink.

<<ava "If you want to… you can try logging in alone tonight." >>

My breath caught.

<<leo "Just me?" >>

She nodded, fingers twisting the ribbon tighter.

<<ava "Only if you’re curious! I mean today was your first time seeing all that too and maybe it would help if you… explored a little?" >>

She swallowed.

<<ava "I think… I’d feel less scared if one of us knew what to expect." >>

She added quickly:

<<ava "But don’t go too far! Just like… movement… walking… looking around…" >>

Her words trailed off into a tiny embarrassed squeak.

<<ava "It would help me. Knowing you’re comfortable there." >>

I stepped closer. She didn’t shy away she just looked up at me with tired, hopeful eyes.

<<leo "I can do that. I’ll take a look inside. Nothing big. I promise." >>

Her shoulders relaxed again, and she let out a soft breath she’d been holding.

<<ava "Thank you…" >>

She reached out, touching my sleeve lightly.

<<ava "You always make things feel… less heavy." >>

I brushed my knuckles gently against her hand.

<<leo "Get some rest, Ava." >>

She nodded sleepily.

<<ava "Call me after you get home…? Just so I know you’re safe?" >>

<<leo "Of course." >>

She smiled small, warm, fading at the edges as exhaustion overtook her.

<<ava "Goodnight… Leo." >>

I lingered a moment, then stepped out of her room quietly, leaving her to rest. Behind the door, I heard the soft click of her ribbon hitting the floor the sound she made only when she truly let herself relax and I walked back toward my dorm, the VR case waiting in my hand… and curiosity warming in my chest.

[[Go to Dorm Room|day_4_20]]


:: day_4_20
<<set $locationImage = "images/locations/leo_dorm.jpeg">>
My dorm felt too quiet when I stepped inside. The door clicked shut behind me, locking the day out… but not my thoughts.

I set the VR case on my desk. It looked almost unreal sitting there like something from the future had followed me home. I stared at it for a long moment.

<<leo "…Should I?" >>

Saying it out loud didn’t help. I was tired. Bone-tired. The kind of tired that sits in your chest, not your muscles.

I rubbed both hands over my face and flopped onto the bed. The dream flickered in my head again Leona’s breath, Ava’s transformed voice, sensations that didn’t belong to my body but still pulsed under my skin.

<<leo "God… not now." >>

I sat up, elbows on knees. Ava’s voice echoed from earlier, “It would help me… knowing you’re comfortable there.” I exhaled slowly.

<<leo "Yeah. But… what if I’m not?" >>

I looked at the case again. The Lumira logo shimmered softly on its surface.

Part of me whispered: Just log in. Just look around. Just for a minute. Another part whispered louder: She trusted you. Don’t screw this up. Don’t explore something she’s afraid of without her. I leaned back into the pillow, trying to clear my mind.

<<leo "Ava’s exhausted… and honestly… so am I." >>

I closed my eyes. Everything today had been beautiful but heavy the fitting room, the embarrassment at the sex shop, the VR emotion maps, the scanning pods, her tiny trembling hand in mine. She pushed herself so hard.

I didn’t want to take even one step further ahead of her than she was ready for.

I set the phone down. Stared at the VR case one last time. Walked over. Placed my hand on top of it. Then shook my head gently.

[[Wait till Tomorrow|leo_dorm_room_night]] | [[Login Tonight|day_4_21_les]]


:: day_4_15_eidolon

The moment the agent tapped the panel, the hologram exploded into neon. Chrome towers. Electric rain. Hover bikes slicing through magenta fog. Holograms blinking across skyscrapers like living graffiti. Ava’s hand flew to her mouth.

<<ava "…Oh my god." >>

My pulse jumped too. The header flashed across the glowing skyline:

<span style="color: red; font-size: 30px;">EIDOLON CITY  -  CYBERPUNK SANDBOX EXPERIENCE</span>

Jamie whistled.

<<jamie "This one’s my favorite. Sexy cyberpunk with emotional intelligence." >>

Rowan clutched his chest dramatically.

<<rowan "Jamie. Cyberpunk already has emotional intelligence." >>

<<jamie "Your avatar seduced a vending machine." >>

<<rowan "WITH PASSION." >>

Ava giggled small and starstruck as the hologram pulled us deeper into the city. A neon street market shimmered in the rain, avatars browsing stalls of glowing tech mods, neon fashion, interface tattoos, cyber pets blinking with pixel eyes.

<<ava "It feels… alive." >>

<<agent "Eidolon adapts to your emotional temperature. If you're anxious, crowds part, lights dim, sound softens. If you’re confident, the world pulses with you." >>

Ava’s fingers crept back into mine.

<<ava "It reacts to feelings?" >>

<<agent "Always." >>

A graffiti-lit alley replaced the market violet, cyan, electric green. Two avatars walked close; their fingerprints left glowing trails on the walls. Their silhouettes brushed and the graffiti flared brighter, exploding into animated neon blossoms. Ava let out a tiny, awed sound.

<<ava "So if you’re close to someone… the city shows it?" >>

<<agent "Yes. Intimacy here is environmental. The world celebrates it, never pressures it." >>

Next, the rooftop bar appeared glass floors, floating tables, a DJ suspended midair on holograms. Rain sparkled around the avatars like digital dust. Ava stared, mesmerized.

<<ava "It’s… beautiful." >>

<<leo "Beautiful and loud." >>

She nudged me, cheeks warm. Then the agent revealed the real heart of the system:

<<agent "Eidolon features emotional bonding, partner resonance, and optional sensual modules that activate only when both avatars show aligned emotional cues." >>

Ava froze not in fear, but in fascination. Rowan leaned close, whispering loudly:

<<rowan "Translation: the city becomes your wingman." >>

Ava squeaked and hid behind her hand. Jamie stroked her back.

<<jamie "It’s slow-burn intimacy. Mood-driven. You never have to do anything you’re not comfortable with." >>

A new scene shimmered into being, Two avatars on a balcony overlooking the entire neon skyline close, breathing slow. The city lights responded by softening, warming, brightening around them like a heartbeat. Ava’s voice was barely audible.

<<ava "It feels… exciting. But still gentle." >>

I stepped closer.

<<leo "Yeah. Like the world gives you space to figure things out." >>

She stared at the city eyes bright, shimmering with awe and something softer.

<<ava "It feels like… the kind of world where you could be brave a little at a time." >>

Her fingers slid fully between mine warm, deliberate.

<<leo "Do you want Eidolon City?" >>

She looked at me, cheeks flushed, breath trembling with anticipation.

<<ava "…Yes." >>

Her smile was shy. Her eyes were glowing.

<<ava "I… want to explore it with you." >>

That was the only choice we needed.

:: day_4_16_eidolon

Ava stared at the neon skyline like it was swallowing her whole. Not with fear mwith wanting. Her fingers tightened between mine.

<<ava "Leo… it’s so  I don’t even have words." >>

<<leo "Yeah. It hits hard." >>

She stepped closer to the hologram, eyes shining in the electric glow.

<<ava "The way it reacts to emotions… that’s what I keep looking at." >>

The graffiti alley replayed two avatars brushing hands, neon flaring like a blush.Ava bit her lip.

<<ava "Do you see how gentle it is? It’s not like… demanding anything. It’s like the world just… listens." >>

<<leo "Exactly. It matches what you feel, not what it thinks you should feel." >>

She nodded quickly relieved someone said it out loud.

<<ava "Yes. Yes, that. It doesn’t assume anything. And the lights they don’t push. They just… wait for you." >>

She glanced up at me.

<<ava "…I think I like that." >>

Jamie folded her arms.

<<jamie "Eidolon is good for slow-burn people. For emotional types. For couples who like space." >>

Rowan added, nodding:

<<rowan "And for awkward nerds who need a whole cyberpunk city to wingman them." >>

Ava turned red.

<<ava "Rowan !" >>

He held up his hands.

<<rowan "Just saying. The city ships you gently." >>

Jamie elbowed him hard. Ava looked at me again. Soft. Brave. Thinking too much and trying not to.

<<ava "How… how does it feel to you, Leo?" >>

I shrugged lightly, stepping closer so our shoulders brushed.

<<leo "It feels like a world where we can take our time. No pressure. Just… exploring together." >>

Ava’s breath stuttered not from panic, but emotion.

<<ava "That’s exactly how it feels to me too." >>

She reached for my sleeve, a tiny tug.

<<ava "Leo… do you want Eidolon?" >>

The neon city reflected across her eyes like tiny stars. I didn’t hesitate.

<<leo "If it feels safe for you, then yeah. I want this one." >>

Ava’s lips parted in a tiny, stunned smile.

<<ava "It feels… safe and exciting. At the same time." >>

She took a small breath, chest rising slowly.

<<ava "Then… let’s pick it. Let’s choose Eidolon City." >>

Her voice trembled not with fear with hope. I squeezed her hand.

<<leo "Then we choose it together." >>

A tiny, glowing smile bloomed across her face quiet, shy, beautiful.

<<ava "…Together." >>

The agent stepped forward, pleased.

<<agent "Eidolon City it is. I’ll prepare the synced gear package." >>

Ava leaned into my arm, still holding my hand tightly.

<<ava "Leo… thank you for helping me decide." >>

<<leo "Always." >>

And under the neon glow of a cyberpunk world waiting for us we chose our first step into intimacy.


:: day_4_17_eidolon


The neon hologram faded, and suddenly the VR store felt real again quiet, glowing, futuristic. Ava still held my hand, her thumb brushing mine lightly, as if grounding herself. The agent nodded with a pleased smile.

<<agent "Eidolon City it is. Let’s take care of your setup." >>

They led us to the counter. A sleek black case was already waiting, glowing faintly with blue interface lines. Ava stared at it like it was a chest of treasure.

<<ava "This is… really happening." >>

<<leo "Yeah. We’re actually doing it." >>

Rowan leaned on the counter dramatically.

<<rowan "I’d like everyone to applaud the brave couple entering neon therapy." >>

Jamie swatted his arm.

<<jamie "Stop making it sound like a cult." >>

<<rowan "I said therapy, not cult. Cults are on Thursdays." >>

Ava laughed soft but the most relaxed she had sounded all day. The Checkout, he agent opened the case, showing the streamlined helmet-visors, the sensory bands, the wrist UIs, and the compact calibration module.

<<agent "This is the Eidolon dual-user kit. Both units are synced to your scans. Any moderate upgrades can be added later." >>

Ava leaned forward slightly.

<<ava "They look… lighter than I expected." >>

<<agent "Designed to reduce sensory fatigue." >>

Rowan tapped the glass.

<<rowan "Translation, they don’t squish your face." >>

Jamie ignored him they’d gotten used to it. I reached for my wallet but Ava touched my hand gently.

<<ava "Leo… can we split it?" >>

Her voice was small but determined. I shook my head.

<<leo "No. I want to do this for us." >>

Her lips parted in a soft, startled breath.

<<ava "O-Oh… okay." >>

Her cheeks warmed, pink under the VR store lights. The agent tapped the register.

<<agent "Your total is " >>

Rowan slapped a card onto the counter like a cowboy in a poker scene.

<<rowan "Use my tournament discount." >>

Jamie yanked him back by the hoodie.

<<jamie "Stop trying to be cool. Let them pay normally." >>

<<rowan "BUT I WON THAT CARD." >>

<<jamie "You cheated with a macro." >>

<<rowan "Skill. It’s called skill." >>

Ava hid behind her hand, giggling. I paid. The terminal beeped. The agent closed the case gently and handed it to me.

<<agent "Your system is ready. Eidolon will be available to launch as soon as you initialize it at home." >>

Ava bowed slightly out of instinct.

<<ava "Th-Thank you…" >>

The agent smiled warmly. Leaving the VR StoreAs the doors slid open with a soft hiss, Ava moved closer not clingy, not afraid, just… close. Her hair brushed my arm. Rowan pointed dramatically after us.

 <<rowan "Farewell, neon lovers! Don’t fry your brains!" >>

<<jamie "ROWAN, STOP TALKING." >>

Ava laughed again, covering her mouth. We stepped into the mall hallway, carrying the sleek black VR case between us like the start of something neither of us knew the shape of yet. Ava looked up at me.

<<ava "Leo?" >>

<<leo "Yeah?" >>

She hesitated then smiled softly.

<<ava "Thank you… for choosing this world with me." >>

I brushed her knuckles with my thumb.

<<leo "Always." >>

She held my hand tighter as we walked toward the mall exit and for the first time all week she looked at peace.

:: day_4_18_eidolon

We stepped out into the cooling evening, mall lights fading behind us. Ava walked close enough that her shoulder brushed mine every few steps. The VR case hung from my hand lighter than it should’ve felt, considering what it meant. Rowan stretched his arms overhead.

<<rowan "Welp! We have completed our sacred duty as emotional support gremlins." >>

Jamie sighed.

<<jamie "Rowan, stop narrating reality." >>

<<rowan "Reality requires commentary." >>

Ava giggled softly beside me, cheeks warm in the dusk.

<<ava "They really don’t stop, do they?" >>

<<leo "Nope. We’ve tried everything." >>

<<ava "Everything?" >>

<<leo "Earplugs. Threats. Hopes. Prayers." >>

She muffled a laugh against her sleeve. Halfway Across Campus, Jamie slowed, tugging Rowan’s sleeve.

<<jamie "This is our turn. We’re heading back to my dorm." >>

<<rowan "Translation: She’s dragging me home because I burned calories helping today." >>

<<jamie "You carried nothing." >>

<<rowan "Emotional labor counts." >>

Ava gave a tiny bow.

<<ava "Thank you… both of you. For coming with us." >>

Jamie softened, brushing Ava’s arm.

<<jamie "You did amazing today, sweetheart." >>

Rowan pointed at me and Ava with mock-seriousness.

<<rowan "Proud of you two. For real. And don’t worry VR is easier than flirting in public." >>

Ava made a tiny squeak.

<<ava "I I wasn’t " >>

<<jamie "He means tomorrow will be fine. You’re not alone in this." >>

Ava nodded, shy and grateful. Rowan raised a hand dramatically.

<<rowan "Farewell, neon couple! May your cyber-city treat you gently!" >>

<<jamie "ROWAN, STOP YELLING GOODBYES." >>

They walked off still bickering, disappearing behind the campus arch. Just Us Again. The quiet settled instantly. Not awkward just soft. Ava exhaled.

<<ava "It feels… quieter now." >>

<<leo "Too quiet?" >>

She shook her head quickly.

<<ava "No. Just… peaceful." >>

Then, hesitantly, gently she slipped her hand back into mine.

<<ava "I like walking with you." >>

The campus lights flickered on, illuminating the path ahead. We walked forward, hand in hand, toward her dorm and the night that waited for us there quiet, warm, full of possibility.


:: day_4_19_eidolon

Ava walked beside me all the way to her dorm, steps slow and quiet, her hand still tucked gently in mine. When we reached the entrance, she hesitated then tugged lightly on my sleeve.

<<ava "Um… could you… walk me up? Just to the door?" >>

<<leo "Yeah. Of course." >>

We climbed the stairs in silence, the air warm with that soft tiredness that follows long days. When we reached her door, she let out a tiny breath and pressed her back to it. Her ribbon was a little crooked. Her cheeks were flushed from walking. She looked exhausted but in a sweet, peaceful way.

<<ava "Today was… a lot." >>

<<leo "Good a lot? Bad a lot?" >>

She shook her head, smiling faintly.

<<ava "Good. Really good. Just… my body feels like I’ve been awake for three days." >>

<<leo "Yeah… same." >>

She curled her fingers around the door handle, but didn’t go in yet.

<<ava "I know we bought the VR set and everything but…" >>

She bit her lip a soft, apologetic motion.

<<ava "Can we… try it tomorrow? I want to be awake enough to actually enjoy it with you." >>

My chest loosened a little. Relief. Understanding.

<<leo "Of course. We don’t have to rush anything." >>

She nodded again, then glanced at the case in my hand.

<<ava "But if you’re… um… curious…" >>

She fidgeted, tapping her toe lightly against her door.

<<ava "You can log in tonight. If you want. Just to look around. I-It might help me too if you’re familiar with it." >>

I blinked.

<<leo "You’re okay with that?" >>

<<ava "Mm… yes. As long as you don’t… go too far without me." >>

Her voice softened at the edges, shy but earnest.

<<ava "I want our first real moment in there to… be together." >>

Heat fluttered in my stomach but I kept my expression steady. I nodded.

<<leo "I promise. I won’t do anything big without you." >>

She relaxed visibly, shoulders dropping.

<<ava "Thank you…" >>

Then her gaze lingered on me warm, grateful, a little embarrassed.

<<ava "Good night, Leo." >>

<<leo "Good night, Ava." >>

She slipped inside, the door closing with a soft click and I stood there for a moment, holding the VR case, thinking about her voice, her smile and her request Don’t go too far without me.


:: day_4_20_eidolon

My dorm felt colder than usual when I stepped inside. Quiet. Dim. Too empty after spending the whole day wrapped in Ava’s warmth and nerves and laughter. I set the VR case on my desk. It made a dull thunk way heavier than it looked.

<<leo "…Okay. Don’t think about it too much." >>

But my brain didn’t listen. I sat on the edge of my bed, elbows on my knees, staring at the black case like it might open itself. Ava’s voice drifted back in… “If you’re curious… you can log in. Just don’t go too far.”

Heat tightened in my chest not sexual, just… emotional. Like something important was waiting. I rubbed my face with both hands.

<<leo "God, I’m tired…" >>

My whole body felt heavy the mall, the bowling, the VR store, the dream, the way Ava grabbed my sleeve at every loud sound…Too much for one day. But then I glanced at the case again. Curiosity poked at me.

<<leo "Maybe just the menu screen?" >>

I reached out Then stopped halfway, fingers hovering above the latch.

<<leo "…Would she be upset?" >>

The room didn’t answer. Obviously. I lay back on the bed, staring at the ceiling, trying to untangle the knot inside me.

Two thoughts fought in my head, Check it now. Just a little. She said it might help her. orcDon’t. Wait for her. Make the first step something you share.

<<leo "…What am I even scared of?" >>

I knew the answer. Not the tech. Not the VR. Ava. Or rather… losing the fragile peacefulness she had today. I exhaled slowly.

<<leo "Okay…" >>

I sat up again, finally deciding. I placed my hand on the VR case, Paused and whispered to myself,

<<leo "...Do I really want to do this alone?" >>

That’s where I stopped. On the edge. The headset unopened. My exhaustion pulling me toward sleep… My curiosity pulling me toward VR… and Ava’s voice, gentle, hopeful, pulling me toward tomorrow.

